From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 08:56:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bonito: include the Lineage libion sepolicy

system/sepolicy 9b2d37dc2 (Android 17) dropped the /dev/ion file_contexts
entry and every coredomain ion_device rule. This kernel's gralloc, Adreno
and QSEECom all allocate through /dev/ion, so with the node labeled
`device` surfaceflinger, keymaster and gatekeeper abort on open (avc
denied read, tclass chr_file). device/lineage/sepolicy/libion carries the
removed rules; include it the way the other legacy Lineage devices do.
---
 BoardConfigLineage.mk | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/BoardConfigLineage.mk b/BoardConfigLineage.mk
index fcb5ecfa..7baf7ada 100644
--- a/BoardConfigLineage.mk
+++ b/BoardConfigLineage.mk
@@ -45,6 +45,8 @@ endif
 # SELinux
 BOARD_SEPOLICY_DIRS += device/google/bonito/sepolicy-lineage/dynamic
 BOARD_SEPOLICY_DIRS += device/google/bonito/sepolicy-lineage/vendor
+# ION labeling and coredomain rules left system/sepolicy in Android 17 (9b2d37dc2); this kernel has no dmabuf heaps
+include device/lineage/sepolicy/libion/sepolicy.mk
 
 # Verified Boot
 ifneq (,$(AVB_CUSTOM_KEY_PATH))
